{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b980f80b-669e-4771-9dde-fd9dcf4d743b","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A normal distribution is symmetric and bell-shaped. Its center is the mean, and its width is measured by the standard deviation.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"The 68–95–99.7 rule"},{"op":"equation","id":"standardize","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"z=\\frac{x-\\mu}{\\sigma}"},{"op":"figure","id":"bell","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4,4],"y":[0,0.46],"axes":"edge","x_label":"z (standard deviations)","y_label":"Probability density"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"density","y":"0.39894228*exp(-x^2/2)","domain":[-4,4]},{"kind":"segment","from":[0,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":0},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.435],"text":"mean","size":"small"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"b980f80b-669e-4771-9dde-fd9dcf4d743b","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s2"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b980f80b-669e-4771-9dde-fd9dcf4d743b","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Area under the curve represents probability. About 68 percent lies within one standard deviation of the mean.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"one_band","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":-1,"to":1},{"kind":"segment","from":[-1,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":-1},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[1,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":1},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.16],"text":"68%"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule_one","anchor":{"el":"standardize","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-\\sigma\\leq X\\leq\\mu+\\sigma)\\approx68\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"b980f80b-669e-4771-9dde-fd9dcf4d743b","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b980f80b-669e-4771-9dde-fd9dcf4d743b","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Extending to two standard deviations captures about 95 percent. Each newly included side band contributes about 13.5 percent.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"two_band","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":-2,"to":-1},{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":1,"to":2},{"kind":"segment","from":[-2,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":-2},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":2},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[-1.5,0.09],"text":"13.5%","size":"small"},{"kind":"text","at":[1.5,0.09],"text":"13.5%","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule_two","anchor":{"el":"rule_one","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-2\\sigma\\leq X\\leq\\mu+2\\sigma)\\approx95\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"b980f80b-669e-4771-9dde-fd9dcf4d743b","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s4"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b980f80b-669e-4771-9dde-fd9dcf4d743b","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Within three standard deviations lies about 99.7 percent. Only 0.3 percent remains outside, split equally between the two tails.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"three_band","on":"bell","marks":[{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":-3,"to":-2},{"kind":"shade","under":"density","from":2,"to":3},{"kind":"segment","from":[-3,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":-3},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":[3,0],"to":{"on":"density","x":3},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[-3.1,0.05],"text":"0.15% tail","size":"small"},{"kind":"text","at":[3.1,0.05],"text":"0.15% tail","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"rule_three","anchor":{"el":"rule_two","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"P(\\mu-3\\sigma\\leq X\\leq\\mu+3\\sigma)\\approx99.7\\%"}],"checkpoint":null}}
